# First-launch wizard opens via the palette command, navigates through the
# sections, cycles the AI-backend and input-style radios via ← / →, self-
# reports Nerd Font with y/n, then Enter Finishes and persists answers.
# Phase 1 sections 1-3 are keyboard-interactive; sections 4-6 only expose
# detection badges + install stubs, which we don't fire here (they'd spawn
# a Pty pane that this test can't easily assert against).

command first_launch.show
expect screen contains "First-launch setup"

# Section 1 (AI ghost-text) is focused on open. All three options render.
expect screen contains "AI ghost-text"
expect screen contains "Claude API"
expect screen contains "Local model"
expect screen contains "Skip for now"

# Cycle to "local" via ↑ → ↑ path — first Right picks "claude-api", second
# picks "local", third picks "skip". We just verify one arrow reaches
# the first choice (proves the radio-cycle plumbing works).
key right
expect screen contains "Claude API"

# Move to section 2 (Input style) with ↓ / j. vim is the pre-populated
# default (from the shipped config), so it should already be selected.
key down
expect screen contains "Input style"
expect screen contains "vim"
expect screen contains "standard"

# Cycle to standard via →.
key right
expect screen contains "standard"

# Move down to section 3 (Nerd Font). Sample glyphs render + two options.
key down
expect screen contains "Nerd Font"
expect screen contains "Sample glyphs"

# y quick-answers "Render as icons".
key y

# Esc = Ask me later; overlay closes, `[ui] first_launch_complete` stays
# false. Reopen via first_launch.show to prove idempotence.
key esc
expect screen lacks "First-launch setup"
command first_launch.show
expect screen contains "First-launch setup"

# Finish this time — Enter.
key enter
expect screen lacks "First-launch setup"
